/*
:name: aeg_xor_bool_one
:type: lec
*/
// PYROPE-vs-PYROPE group, the fixture of the aegraph rule `xor_bool_one`
// (pass/aegraph/rules/arith.rules): `x ^ 1 = EQ(x, 0)` for a 0/1 value x. tolg
// lowers `a != 0` to `(a == 0) ^ 1`, a Xor over a comparison, so the rule's
// 0/1 guard (bool01) holds. This is the REFERENCE, compiled by the classic
// engine; `aeg_xor_bool_one_1.prp` is the same source compiled by the e-graph
// engine, which must prove equal AND must have made the rule do the work.
pub comb top(a:U8, b:U8) -> (y:Bool, z:Bool) {
  y = a != 0
  z = (a == b) != true
}
